<title>SOUTH KOREA: Kia Motors union workers walk out.</title>
<headline>Kia Motors union workers walk out.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union workers at Kia Motors, South Korea's second largest carmaker, began an indefinite strike on Thursday in protest at the passage of a new labour law, a union official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We began the strike this morning,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The Kia union is affiliated to the outlawed Korea Confederation of Trade Unions, which called out all its 500,000 members on Thursday shortly after the ruling party rammed through parliament a labour bill allowing worker layoffs and flexible working hours.</p>
</text>
